<div class="page">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <div class="section-title">Instructions for Recipient</div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Recipient's taxpayer identification number (TIN). For your protection, this form may show only the last four digits of your TIN (SSN, ITIN, or EIN).
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Account number. May show an account or other unique number the payer assigned to your account.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Address. May show a mailing address or a physical address.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      The amount shown may be divided proportionally to you as a participant or beneficiary of a partnership in an employee stock ownership plan (ESOP) or a similar entity.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 2a. Total capital gain distributions represents the total amount of capital gain distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 2b. Unrecap. Sec. 1250 gain represents the amount of gain distributions that are not subject to the unrecaptured Section 1250 gain tax rate.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 2c. Section 1202 gain represents the amount of gain distributions that are subject to the Section 1202 gain tax rate.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 2d. Collectibles (89i) gain represents the amount of gain distributions from collectibles that are subject to the collectibles gain tax rate.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 2e. Section 897 ordinary dividends represents the amount of ordinary dividends to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 2f. Section 897 capital gain represents the amount of capital gain distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 3. Nondividend distributions represents the amount of distributions to you that are not dividends.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 4. Federal income tax withheld represents the amount of federal income tax withheld from the distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 5. Section 199A dividends represents the amount of dividends to you that are subject to the Section 199A tax.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 6. Investment expenses represents the amount of investment expenses paid on your behalf.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 7. Foreign tax paid represents the amount of foreign tax paid on your behalf.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 8. Foreign country or U.S. possession represents the country or U.S. possession where the income was earned.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 9. Cash liquidation distributions represents the amount of cash distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 10. Noncash liquidation distributions represents the amount of noncash distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 11. FATCA filing requirement indicates whether the payer has filed a FATCA form for you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 12. Exempt-interest dividends represents the amount of dividends to you that are exempt from tax.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 13. Specified private activity bond interest dividends represents the amount of interest distributions to you from specified private activity bonds.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <div class="section-title">Instructions for Payer</div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 1. Shows the payer's name, street address, city or town, state or province, country, and ZIP or foreign postal code.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 2. Shows the portion of the amount in Box 1a that may be eligible for the unrecaptured Section 1250 gain tax rate.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 3. Shows the amount you are dividing proportionally to you as a participant or beneficiary of a partnership in an employee stock ownership plan (ESOP) or a similar entity.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 4. Shows the federal income tax withheld from the distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 5. Shows the amount of dividends to you that are subject to the Section 199A tax.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 6. Shows the amount of investment expenses paid on your behalf.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 7. Shows the foreign tax paid on your behalf.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 8. Shows the country or U.S. possession where the income was earned.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 9. Shows the amount of cash distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 10. Shows the amount of noncash distributions to you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 11. Indicates whether the payer has filed a FATCA form for you.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 12. Shows the amount of dividends to you that are exempt from tax.
    </div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Box 13. Shows the amount of interest distributions to you from specified private activity bonds.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <div class="section-title">Notes</div>
    <div class="instruction-text">
      Notes: Boxes 2e and 2f apply only to foreign persons and entities whose income is not subject to U.S. tax.
    </div>
